{"tag":"XVJZ","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"theorem-1","file":"","number":"1","section":"sec-1","order":1,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"The Euler--Mascheroni constant $\\gamma$, arising as the finite part of\n$\\zeta(1)$, admits a natural extension to an infinite family of\nregularized functionals $g_n(x)$.\nThey admit explicit integral representations, differential and\nladder relations, and a unified umbral generating function, thereby situating\n$\\gamma$ within a broader analytic framework.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","name":"Main Theorem","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":85,"to":92},"hash":"sha256:6d75c253f92713c5c0c7835cfb26e668ba1716b87648eff1d7d4141f136683b3","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"5YBN","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"prop-1","file":"","number":"1","section":"sec-2","order":2,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"For $n\\ge1$ and $x\u003e0$,\n\\[\ng_n(x)=H_n-\\log(2\\pi x)\n- n \\int_0^1 (1-u)^{n-1}\\,\\log\\!\\bigl(2\\sin(\\pi x u)\\bigr)\\,du.\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"prop","number_from":"render","name":"Integral representation","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":106,"to":112},"hash":"sha256:0fd156dea6ceadab0708737efb068d5527b60f1833058b1baa648ebf941b537b","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"22QV","kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"corollary-1","file":"","number":"1","section":"sec-2","order":3,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"For $n\\ge1$,\n\\[\ng_n(x) = O(x^2)\\qquad (x\\to 0^+).\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"corollary","item":"statement/corollary","head":"environment","counter":"corollary","number_from":"render","name":"Small-$x$ normalization","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":114,"to":119},"hash":"sha256:d13abf7bd3d375958fa5274ffe9ef3ce9d740a284d6b713fafc33d4b510910a3","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"L77X","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"prop-2","file":"","number":"2","section":"sec-2","order":4,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"For $n\\ge1$ and $x\u003e0$,\n\\begin{align*}\nx\\,g_n'(x)\n\u0026= 2n!\\sum_{m\\ge1}\\frac{(2m)!}{(2m+n)!}\\,\\zeta(2m)\\,x^{2m} - 1\\\\\n\u0026= -\\,n \\int_0^1 (1-u)^{n-1}\\,\\pi x u\\,\\cot(\\pi x u)\\,du \\;-\\; 1.\n\\end{align*}","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"prop","number_from":"render","name":"Differential form","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":121,"to":128},"hash":"sha256:3f2d50992f1c0bb5eb4d7172546b5f202780e203996648e025723ee02b3ad18d","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"KMSY","kind":"remark","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"remark-1","file":"","number":"1","section":"sec-2","order":5,"title":"Remark","body_md":"The derivative formula shows that $g_n$ is governed by cotangent averages,\nlinking it with classical Bernoulli expansions of $\\pi\\cot(\\pi z)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"remark","item":"remark","head":"environment","counter":"remark","number_from":"render","name":"Cotangent connection","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":130,"to":133},"hash":"sha256:3a82bb764cf630b8ff8dfe9a466b56bb587810106dcd0cb896fdb04be539cd08","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"EKR3","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"prop-3","file":"","number":"3","section":"sec-2","order":6,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"For $n\\ge1$ and $x\u003e0$,\n\\[\ng_{n+1}(x)-g_n(x)\n=\\frac{1}{n+1}\n- \\int_0^1\\!\\bigl[(n+1)(1-u)^n-n(1-u)^{n-1}\\bigr]\\,\n\\log(2\\sin(\\pi x u))\\,du.\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"prop","number_from":"render","name":"Ladder in $n$","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":135,"to":143},"hash":"sha256:95d0a8189c01599e56cf03fd4560c06eb287a854f9b38216108e105408015418","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"GMAE","kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"corollary-2","file":"","number":"2","section":"sec-2","order":7,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"For fixed $x\u003e0$,\n\\[\ng_n(x) = O\\!\\left(\\tfrac{1}{n}\\right)\\qquad (n\\to\\infty).\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"corollary","item":"statement/corollary","head":"environment","counter":"corollary","number_from":"render","name":"Large-$n$ decay","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":145,"to":150},"hash":"sha256:86be7476c45dada6db1c3dc4101e52df7c36555065ecd94531561cbf5ccd0909","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-7","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"VLSQ","kind":"remark","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"remark-2","file":"","number":"2","section":"sec-3","order":8,"title":"Remark","body_md":"Thus $g_n(x)$ interpolates between the Euler--Mascheroni constant\nand higher Bernoulli data, reflecting the classical bridge\nbetween Clausen sums and even zeta values.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"remark","item":"remark","head":"environment","counter":"remark","number_from":"render","name":"Bernoulli connection","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":167,"to":171},"hash":"sha256:f8d60ecb7e723ee5d7da6b5aab6be6828a12095e1cdaae1c5a61c8ef4f3772d3","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-8","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"UIHZ","kind":"remark","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"remark-3","file":"","number":"3","section":"sec-3","order":9,"title":"Remark","body_md":"In the cosine--Clausen expansion one encounters\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Cl}^{(c)}_{2m+1}(\\theta)\n= \\sum_{r=0}^{m-1}\\zeta(2m+1-2r)\\,\\frac{(-1)^r \\theta^{2r}}{(2r)!}\n - \\frac{(-1)^m \\theta^{2m}}{(2m)!}\\,g_{2m}\\!\\Bigl(\\tfrac{|\\theta|}{2\\pi}\\Bigr)\n + \\cdots,\n\\]\nwhere the divergent central contribution involving $\\zeta(1)$\nis naturally replaced by $g_{2m}(|\\theta|/2\\pi)$.\nThis indicates that the family $g_n(x)$ has its origin\nin the same mechanism that produces the Euler--Mascheroni constant\nin the simplest case $m=0$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"remark","item":"remark","head":"environment","counter":"remark","number_from":"render","name":"Clausen origin","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":174,"to":187},"hash":"sha256:287a74307393ae43ac50117e0f59bfa53a6e9cebcfa2d6808f7ecd4beafc2301","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-9","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"QNRT","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"prop-4","file":"","number":"4","section":"sec-4","order":10,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"For $|z|\u003c1$,\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{n\\ge1} g_n(x)\\,z^n\n\u0026= -\\,\\frac{z}{1-z}\\,\\log(2\\pi x)\n   - \\frac{\\log(1-z)}{1-z} \\\\\n\u0026\\quad - \\int_0^1 \\log\\!\\bigl(2\\sin(\\pi x u)\\bigr)\\,\n      \\frac{z}{\\bigl(1 - z(1-u)\\bigr)^2}\\,du.\n\\end{align*}","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"prop","number_from":"render","name":"Generating function","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":193,"to":202},"hash":"sha256:b8d2c3103ecd629fea0fbd77248a015cede4c17ffa04da0c697c661941c37db2","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-10","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"H2PB","kind":"remark","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"remark-4","file":"","number":"4","section":"sec-4","order":11,"title":"Remark","body_md":"The generating function realizes $g_n(x)$\nas coefficients of an operator-valued series\nacting on $\\log(2\\sin(\\pi x u))$.\nThis matches the umbral perspective\n\\cite{Roman1984,RotaTaylor1994,Blasiak2005},\nwhere moments are encoded by a single parent functional.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"remark","item":"remark","head":"environment","counter":"remark","number_from":"render","name":"Umbral perspective","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":204,"to":211},"hash":"sha256:ddac84e9d413e9fef67d24ee794fe2115aa5a91fb33d96ff605d896462e5ba66","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#env-11","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"D9OZ","kind":"proof","paper":"2509.22289","version":"1","local":"proof-1","file":"","section":"sec-5","order":12,"title":"Proof","body_md":"The defining moment representation of $g_n(x)$\nleads directly to the integral identity in Proposition~2.1.\nDifferentiating under the integral sign yields\nthe differential and ladder relations.\nFinally, the umbral generating function provides a\nunified operator perspective, from which the Main Theorem follows\nby a straightforward synthesis.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proof","item":"proof","head":"environment","name":"Sketch of proof","scope":"paper","flags":["orphan"],"span":{"file":"backup00_beyond_gamma_v1.0.tex","from":219,"to":227},"hash":"sha256:26c66fcb87ebb10fbbd488eb9147b9fa1359574bb7fa8e8f48b0ad96828c8beb","minhash":"","census":"2509.22289v1#proof-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
